  "Question": "The five tires of a car (four road tires and a full-sized spare) were rotated so that each tire was used the same number of miles during the first \\(30{,}000\\) miles the car traveled. For how many miles was each tire used?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6000\\)",
    "B": "\\(7500\\)",
    "C": "\\(24{,}000\\)",
    "D": "\\(30{,}000\\)",
    "E": "\\(37{,}500\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "For every mile the car travels, four tires are each used for one mile. Thus, during the first \\(30{,}000\\) miles, the combined use of all the tires is\n\\[\n4\\cdot30{,}000=120{,}000\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nSince the five tires share this use equally, each tire is used for\n\\[\n120{,}000\\div5=24{,}000\\text{ miles}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(24{,}000\\) miles, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
